---@class clickhouse_cloud.service.UpdateServiceReplicaScalingRequest
---@field organizationId string ID of the organization that owns the service.
---@field serviceId string ID of the service to update scaling parameters.
---@field minReplicaMemoryGb? number Minimum auto-scaling memory in Gb for a single replica. Available only for 'production' services. Must be a multiple of 4 and greater than or equal to 8. A range in vertical autoscaling; equal to maxReplicaMemoryGb in horizontal.
---@field maxReplicaMemoryGb? number Maximum auto-scaling memory in Gb for a single replica. Available only for 'production' services. Must be a multiple of 4 and lower than or equal to 120 for non paid services or 356 for paid services. A range in vertical autoscaling; equal to minReplicaMemoryGb in horizontal.
---@field autoscalingMode? clickhouse_cloud.service.UpdateServiceReplicaScalingRequestAutoscalingMode|string Target autoscaling mode. Omit to keep the service on its current mode. "vertical" runs a fixed replica count while memory scales between minReplicaMemoryGb and maxReplicaMemoryGb; "horizontal" scales the replica count between minReplicas and maxReplicas at a fixed per-replica memory (minReplicaMemoryGb equal to maxReplicaMemoryGb). Switching to horizontal requires the feature to be enabled for the organization.
---@field numReplicas? number Fixed replica count for vertical autoscaling (autoscalingMode "vertical"). Mutually exclusive with minReplicas/maxReplicas. When switching to vertical (autoscalingMode "vertical") with numReplicas and no memory, the service's stored baseline per-replica memory is kept as the new vertical range.
---@field minReplicas? number Minimum number of replicas. A minReplicas/maxReplicas band scales the replica count in horizontal autoscaling (autoscalingMode "horizontal"). Must be provided together with maxReplicas. Mutually exclusive with numReplicas. Requires horizontal autoscaling to be enabled for the service, unless autoscalingMode is omitted or "vertical" and minReplicas equals maxReplicas (an equal band is then an accepted vertical fixed count and needs no horizontal entitlement).
---@field maxReplicas? number Maximum number of replicas. A minReplicas/maxReplicas band scales the replica count in horizontal autoscaling (autoscalingMode "horizontal"). Must be provided together with minReplicas. Mutually exclusive with numReplicas. Requires horizontal autoscaling to be enabled for the service, unless autoscalingMode is omitted or "vertical" and minReplicas equals maxReplicas (an equal band is then an accepted vertical fixed count and needs no horizontal entitlement).
---@field idleScaling? boolean When set to true the service is allowed to scale down to zero when idle. True by default.
---@field idleTimeoutMinutes? number Set minimum idling timeout (in minutes). Must be >= 5 minutes.
---@field profile? string Custom instance profile. Omit to leave the current profile unchanged. Profiles other than v1-default and v2-default are only available for ENTERPRISE and BYOC organization tiers. Standard values: 'v1-default', 'v2-default', 'v1-highmem-xs', 'v1-highmem-s', 'v1-highmem-m', 'v1-highmem-l', 'v1-highmem-xl'. A BYOC profile (e.g. 'v1-standard-byoc-16') is a pin: minReplicaMemoryGb and maxReplicaMemoryGb must both be sent and equal that profile's memory size, and a memory range cannot be combined with it. To move a pinned BYOC service to a memory range, send the range without a profile, or with 'v1-default'. A non-BYOC custom profile other than v2-default cannot be combined with a memory change; send the profile alone to change only the name. The profile cannot switch a service between Gen 1 and Gen 2 hardware (to or from 'v2-default'): the request is rejected with a 400 error; contact support to move it. While a schedule entry is active the new profile is stored on the schedule base config and the running service keeps the entry profile until the window ends. Use the serviceProfiles endpoint to list the profiles available to the organization.

---Target autoscaling mode. Omit to keep the service on its current mode. "vertical" runs a fixed replica count while memory scales between minReplicaMemoryGb and maxReplicaMemoryGb; "horizontal" scales the replica count between minReplicas and maxReplicas at a fixed per-replica memory (minReplicaMemoryGb equal to maxReplicaMemoryGb). Switching to horizontal requires the feature to be enabled for the organization.
---@alias clickhouse_cloud.service.UpdateServiceReplicaScalingRequestAutoscalingMode "vertical"|"horizontal"

