---Set service upgrade window
---
---Creates or fully replaces the upgrade window for a service. The upgrade window currently lasts 6 hours from `startHourUtc`. The upgrade window can only be set on primary services; secondary services inherit the primary service window.
---
---Errors:
---- 400: invalid field values (`weekday` not in 0–6, `startHourUtc` not in {0, 6, 12, 18}), or the service is a secondary service.
---- 401: missing, invalid, or disabled API key.
---- 403: caller lacks `control-plane:service:manage` on the service, or the organization does not have the scheduled upgrades feature enabled.
---- 404: service does not exist or is not visible to the caller.
---
---`PUT /v1/organizations/{organizationId}/services/{serviceId}/upgradeWindow`
---Errors: FeatureUnavailable.
---@param input clickhouse_cloud.service.UpdateUpgradeWindowRequest
---@return clickhouse_cloud.service.UpgradeWindow? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:update_upgrade_window(input) end

---Create or replace service autoscaling schedule
---
---Creates or fully replaces the autoscaling schedule for a service. Pass an empty `entries` array to clear the schedule — a subsequent GET will return 404, and the response will contain an empty `baseConfig` (all fields absent). The base scaling config (applied when no entry is active) is managed separately via the `replicaScaling` endpoint. Requires the scheduled autoscaling feature to be enabled for the organization. Gen 2 (v2-default) services use a fixed size and cannot idle. An entry may leave out fields it takes from the base config, but each entry combined with those fields must have equal minReplicaMemoryGb and maxReplicaMemoryGb, a fixed replica count (numReplicas, or equal minReplicas and maxReplicas), and idling off; otherwise the request is rejected.
---
---`POST /v1/organizations/{organizationId}/services/{serviceId}/scalingSchedule`
---@param input clickhouse_cloud.service.UpsertScalingScheduleRequest
---@return clickhouse_cloud.service.ScalingSchedule? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:upsert_scaling_schedule(input) end

